entry.summary:
The Codebase That Had 130 Grays


I spent four years working in a production codebase that had 130 gray variables. I actually counted them once.
Someone needs a border color, creates $gray-v1. Someone else needs a slightly darker background, doesn't find the right gray in the file — or doesn't bother looking — creates $gray-v2. Four years of that across 5 product modules and this is what you get:
$gray-v12: #6B7280;
$gray-v13: #6E7581;
$gray-v14: #707682;
$gray-v38: #4A5163;
$gray-v39: #4B5264;
$gray-v47: #5C6370;
$gray-v89: #3D4450;

Seven variables. Can you tell them apart by hex value? We couldn't either. $gray-v38 and $gray-v39 differ by one hex digit. They were used on different screens for the same purpose — disabled text. Created six months apart by two different developers who had …
